  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Atlantic mackerel and JAR through the intermediary of Garcimangosone D. Both the Immunoglobulin lambda-like polypeptide 1 and Shiga-like toxin 1 subunit B are targets of Garcimangosone D, and each of these entities is linked to Atlantic mackerel. This indicates that Garcimangosone D may act as a common mediator in the biological pathway leading from Atlantic mackerel to JAR. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but further validation would be needed to confirm the direct interaction between Atlantic mackerel and JAR. The mechanism appears to involve Garcimangosone D as a key player in the interaction, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated.",
